  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><title><span>Warm Up Activity</span></title>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem id="prob-00001">
    <para id="para-00001">Study the table. What do you notice? What do you wonder?</para>
    
    <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00001">
      <tgroup cols="7"><tbody><row>
          <entry><emphasis>
            \(x\)
          </emphasis></entry><entry>
            0
          </entry>
          <entry>
            1
          </entry>
          <entry>
            2
          </entry>
          <entry>
            3
          </entry>
          <entry>
            4
          </entry>
          <entry>
            5
          </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><emphasis>
            \(y\)
          </emphasis></entry><entry>
            0
          </entry>
          <entry>
            16
          </entry>
          <entry>
            64
          </entry>
          <entry>
            144
          </entry>
          <entry>
            256
          </entry>
          <entry>
            400
          </entry>
        </row>
      </tbody></tgroup></table>
    
    
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00001">
    
    <para id="para-00002">Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para id="para-00003">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00004">Things you may notice:</para>
    
    <list id="list-00001">
      <item> The \(x\)-values increment by 1 as you move across the table.</item>
      <item> The \(y\)-values increase.</item>
      <item> All \(y\)-values are even and divisible by 4, 8, and 16.</item>
      <item> The \(y\)-values are all perfect squares.</item>
      <item> The successive differences between the \(y\)-values are growing.</item>
    </list>
    
    <para id="para-00005">Things you may wonder:</para>
    
    <list id="list-00002">
      <item> Is there a rule for these numbers?</item>
      <item> Do the numbers represent the growth of a geometric pattern?</item>
      <item> Do the numbers represent a quadratic relationship?</item>
      <item> What is the next number in the table?</item>
    </list>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
